{
  "_what": "A build artefact mapping the city text that media guides print in an opponent column to a club nickname. Guides overwhelmingly print CITIES, not nicknames.",
  "_NOT_EVIDENCE": "There is deliberately no source_id and no source field. Nothing may cite this file as evidence for any claim. It exists so a measurement can decide whether two rows are about the same fixture; it is a lookup, not a finding. Same standing as export/position_labels.json.",
  "_the_central_problem": "A city names a FRANCHISE ONLY WITHIN A PERIOD. Baltimore is the Colts until 1983 and the Ravens from 1996. Chicago is the Bears or the Cardinals before 1960. Disambiguating therefore requires the year -- and in the mirror measurement the year is the unknown. Resolving an ambiguous city by a carried-forward year would be circular and would MANUFACTURE the agreement being measured.",
  "_the_rule": "Ambiguous cities are DROPPED, never guessed. Dropping can only understate mirror coverage, never overstate it. The drop count is reported by decade so the headroom is visible alongside the floor.",

